Spec: Editor Module

Purpose:
  Canvas orchestration layer — connects tools, rendering, input, history,
  and snapping into a cohesive editing experience.

Structure:
  ./controller.ts: Central CanvasController class
  ./tool-manager.ts: Tool switching and delegation
  ./input.ts: Mouse, keyboard, wheel, pan input handling
  ./history.ts: Undo/redo stack with auto-save trigger
  ./snapping.ts: Snap point detection (endpoints, midpoints, grid, material)
  ./render/renderer.ts: Canvas 2D rendering (grid, shapes, selection, nodes, snap markers)
  ./Canvas.tsx: React component wrapping the HTML canvas

Owns:
  ./controller.ts
  ./tool-manager.ts
  ./input.ts
  ./history.ts
  ./snapping.ts
  ./render/**
  ./Canvas.tsx

Must:
  Render at most once per animation frame (rAF batching).
  Only trigger React re-renders when selectedIds actually change.
  Dispose all event listeners on unmount (no memory leaks).
  InputManager supports zoom-at-point via mouse wheel.
  SnapManager detects endpoints, midpoints, centers, material edges, and grid.
  History stack is limited to 50 entries.

Must not:
  Directly modify shape data — always delegate to commands.
  Re-render the canvas on every Zustand state change (only canvas-relevant changes).
  Use requestAnimationFrame polling loops (use on-demand rendering).

Depends on:
  @CanvasRenderer
  @ToolManager
  @InputManager
  @HistoryManager
  @SnapManager
  @useStore
